CORE
main.c
--inline
^\[(main\.)?assertion\.1\] .*enum argument reinterpreted: SUCCESS$
^\[(main\.)?assertion\.2\] .*double argument is nondet: FAILURE$
argument type does not match parameter 'x', inserting non-deterministic value
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^Invariant check failed
--
Calls whose argument types differ from the parameter types made the inliner
fail an invariant. Arguments that symbolic execution reinterprets (here an
enum) must give the same result after inlining; other arguments (here a
double) are replaced by a non-deterministic value.
